**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests`

**How to implement.** Main and Inverse open a kit the user picks, and each constructor window works in its kit until it closes (the S4.3 brief: Program.fs MainConstructorWindow and InverseConstructorWindow take a KitContext; the Launcher's Main and Inverse open a kit through the KitFolderPicker seam, followed by S4.1's initialise-or-open; headless tests substitute the seam with a folder under the test output; .spec-md §3.10; §10.5: Close kit loses nothing, because kit writes are immediate and atomic). In `OpticalConstructor.App/Program.fs`: (1) `MainConstructorWindow(context : AppContext, opened : OpenedKit)` and `InverseConstructorWindow(context : AppContext, opened : OpenedKit)`: the opened kit (step 150) carries the `KitContext` (`opened.library.kit`) with what was read when it opened, because a window cannot fail and the reads and the resolution precede it. `ConstructorScene` gains `storesOf (context : AppContext) (opened : OpenedKit) : KitLibraryStores`, `{ library = context.library; materials = context.materials; samples = context.samples; categories = context.categories }.overlaidWith opened.overlay` (step 142), so the kit's snapshot entries resolve in its window. Each window's seed is today's (`initMainWith` / `initInverse` over those four stores and `context.experiments`, with the record update threading `sources`, `experimentExport`, `libraryBackups` and `catalogueImports`), then `.loadKit opened` (step 152). When the window closes (`Closed`) it releases the kit (`opened.library.kit.close ()`); an `Error e` is logged with `Logger.logError` carrying `e.describe`. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3. (2) `LauncherWindow(locations, settings, opened, pickerFor : TopLevel -> KitFolderPicker)` (steps 88, 89, 112): the new argument builds the folder picker over the launcher, and `App.OnFrameworkInitializationCompleted` passes `fun owner -> KitFolderPicker.ofWindow owner Startup.dataLocations.kitsFolder` (step 150; 001 §G: the suggested parent of kit folders). Main and Inverse no longer build a window directly: a click starts `(pickerFor this).pickKitFolder ()` on the UI thread (`Async.StartImmediate`); `None` does nothing; `Some folder` calls one local function of the folder, the mode (`ForwardConstructor` / `InverseConstructor`, `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:ConstructorMode`) and the access, which calls `KitOpening.openKitAt folder access ClockProvider.system (KitAuthor Environment.UserName) context.catalogueImports` with `ReadWriteKitAccess`. On `Ok opened` it shows `MainConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for the forward mode and `InverseConstructorWindow(context, opened)` for the inverse one. On `Error e` no window opens, and the launcher shows, between the title and the surface buttons, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `ConstructorUiId.launcherKitErrorText` as its `Name` and `AutomationId`, reading `The kit could not be opened: <e.describe>`; the next successful open removes it. Steps 155 and 156 call the same local function. Materials and Library are unchanged: they need no kit (001 §F). (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the launcher group (`UiIds.fs:588`): `static member launcherKitErrorText : ConstructorUiId = ConstructorUiId "LauncherKitErrorText"` with a one-line doc. (4) Tests. `TestAppScope` (step 152) gains `kitPickerOf (folder : KitFolder) : KitFolderPicker`, answering `Some folder` at once, with a one-line doc. Every fact that builds a constructor window passes `TestAppScope.openedKitIn` of its module's name over its context's `catalogueImports` and keeps its assertions: `WireUiCompositionTests` (`WireUiCompositionTests.fs:113`), `WireUi0040CompositionTests` (`WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:175`), `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` (`WireUiFinalCompositionTests.fs:120`, `:121`), `AppContextTests`' two-window acceptance (`AppContextTests.fs:137`, `:140`, one kit each), `TableAndElementRotationTests` (`TableAndElementRotationTests.fs:224`) and `LauncherTests`' single-instance fact (`LauncherTests.fs:215`). `MainWorkbenchTests.mainWith` loads its model over `TestAppScope.openedKitIn (FolderName "MainWorkbenchTests")`, so the workbench it mounts has the window's shape (`MainWorkbenchTests.fs:89`). Every `LauncherWindow(...)` in `LauncherTests` and `WireUiFinalCompositionTests` passes `fun _ -> TestAppScope.kitPickerOf (TestAppScope.freshKitFolder <owner>)`. In `LauncherTests`, `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene` and `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene` keep their assertions over a fresh folder and also find `.kit-json` in it. It gains, each with trait `ui-smoke`: `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`: a folder whose kit holds one experiment (written through `openKitAt`, `writeExperiment` and `close`) opens exactly one `MainConstructorWindow`, and closing it removes `.oc/lock`; `a cancelled pick opens nothing`: a picker answering `None` opens no window and creates no folder; and `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`: a folder whose `E1.experiment-json` holds `{` opens no window, shows `launcherKitErrorText` naming `E1.experiment-json`, and holds no `.oc/lock`.

**Acceptance.** After the windows take an opened kit, the launcher's Main and Inverse MUST open the folder the picker answers as a kit (initialising it when needed) in the forward and inverse constructor, show a kit that cannot be opened in `launcherKitErrorText`, and a closed window MUST release its kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the Main button opens the forward Main constructor scene`, `the Inverse button opens the inverse constructor scene`, `the Main button opens the kit the picker answers, with its experiments`, `a cancelled pick opens nothing`, `a kit that cannot be opened is shown on the launcher and opens no window`, the count rising by 3; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
